          "worked": "The possible totals are $\\$2$, $\\$3$ and $\\$4$. Without replacement, four coins remain after the first draw. A total of $\\$3$ can occur in either order.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X=2)&=\\frac35\\times\\frac24=\\frac3{10}\\\\P(X=3)&=\\frac35\\times\\frac24+\\frac25\\times\\frac34=\\frac6{10}\\\\P(X=4)&=\\frac25\\times\\frac14=\\frac1{10}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe probabilities sum to $\\frac3{10}+\\frac6{10}+\\frac1{10}=1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the expected value of $X$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$E(X)=\\frac{14}{5}$ dollars, or $\\$2.80$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}E(X)&=2\\times\\frac3{10}+3\\times\\frac6{10}+4\\times\\frac1{10}\\\\E(X)&=\\frac{28}{10}\\\\E(X)&=\\frac{14}{5}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe expected total value is $\\$2.80$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
